Synth mode (src/synth.c, src/synth_ui.c, src/synth/) uses code and data from Felucca, the firmware by Leo Kuroshita
(@kurogedelic), Hugelton Instruments, https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca (GPL-3.0-only, Felucca-Engines MIT):

  src/synth/fm6_core.c   Felucca's FM6 core, a C port of the msfa engine of Dexed.
            SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0. Copyright 2012 Google Inc.; Copyright 2016-2025 Pascal Gauthier;
            C port for Felucca (integer only) 2026 Leo Kuroshita. Copied unchanged, header kept; the licence text is
            in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.
  src/synth/fm6_tables.h  the tables fm6_core.c needs, as written by Felucca's tools/gen_tables.py (GPL-3.0-only;
            the sine table comes from Felucca-Engines, MIT); not edited.
  src/synth/fm6_factory.h  Felucca's own FM6 factory voices, as written by its tools/gen_fm6_patches.py (GPL-3.0-only).
  src/synth.c   the patch pack / unpack routines follow Felucca's eng_fm6.c (fm6_unpack / fm6_pack, GPL-3.0-only);
            the rest of the file (voices, effects, arpeggiator, DX7 SysEx, parameter-lock overrides, scales and chords,
            mutate, the host voice's settings swap) is new.
  src/synth_seq.c   the sequencer's step model (four notes, NOTE / TIE, velocity, chance), its live recording (Felucca
            seq.c rec_note / rec_hold / rec_release: nearest step, overdub, held notes as TIEs, an early release puts
            the last TIE back, no double trigger) and step entry (ui_input.c seq_entry: a chord into the cursor step,
            letting go moves on) are adapted from Felucca (GPL-3.0-only, Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita); the rest
            (patterns, clock, swing, MIDI clock, storage, the grid editing, parameter locks, the song chain) is new.
  src/synth_ui.c   the scope follows Felucca's HOME scope (fx.c scope_buf, ui_graph.c graph_scope, GPL-3.0-only: a ring
            of every other output sample, a rising zero crossing as the trigger, an auto-scaled 2 px trace); the
            trigger's hysteresis, the slow release of the scale, the strip-wise sending and the other views are new.
  The DX7 voice and bank formats are Yamaha's; no factory ROM data of any instrument is included.

Ideas and rules from Mutable Dreams (version 2.1), the FM-1 firmware by Kid Bunka,
https://github.com/kidbee85-beep/mutable-dreams (its own files: MIT OR GPL-3.0-only, used here under GPL-3.0-only;
no Mutable Instruments code is used). No file of it is copied; these follow its design and are new code:
  src/synth.c   the MIDI learn rules (syn_ml_safe: the CCs that may be learned, as its dsp/midi_learn.inc
            learn_safe; syn_ml_pickup: pick-up / soft takeover as its learn_cc does) and the placement of MIDI in
            within the audio block (syn_timed, syn_midi_frame: its app.c / dsp/dreams.cpp md_block_begin and md_midi_at,
            a constant one-block latency instead of a block of jitter); the morph's drift between two snapshots
            (its dsp/creative.inc drift_capture / creative_tick: A and B, a ping-pong of 10 to 300 s).
  src/synth_learn.c   the learn gesture and bindings around those rules.
  src/synth_gen.c   generators in the spirit of its sequence generators (euclid, sparse, pulse, arp from the
            chord / scale, drift) and its phrase tools (copy, paste, transpose, mirror).
  src/synth_seq.c   trig conditions FIRST / alternating / FILL in spare bits of a step, as its md_step keeps its rule
            in spare bits of chance and gate.
  app/app.c   the overload guard on fm1-base's APP_OVERLOAD hook, as its app_overload / md_overload (ECO) uses it.

Files from fm1-base and felucca-bsp stay under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, file by file; the source of those
files is the submodules at the commits recorded in this repository. MPL-2.0 is compatible with the GPL (its section
3.3). The shape of app/ follows fm1-base's template (base/template/) and the way charlesvestal/fm1-ctl is built on it.
Fonts (Barlow, Terminus) are SIL OFL 1.1, from fm1-base's assets.

RUN4 is the name of an iOS app by the same author; this repository contains no code from it.
